// Christian Religious Education – 42 Questions in GIFT format

// Q1
::Q1:: After Adam and Eve sinned and discovered their nakedness, God made clothes from animal skin for them.  
What attribute of God is shown here? { ~Sole creator ~Organised ~All powerful =Loving }

// Q2
::Q2:: Kate lives with her father and two brothers.  
What kind of family does she come from? { =Nuclear family ~Extended family ~Single parent family ~Non-existent family }

// Q3
::Q3:: Which pair consists of Old Testament books only? { =Leviticus and Malachi ~Acts and Joel ~Ruth and Naomi ~Romans and Philippians }

// Q4
::Q4:: The book of Luke 19:2–10 tells the story of Zacchaeus.  
What lesson do we learn from this story? { =Jesus came to save sinners ~Zacchaeus was a very good man ~It is okay to steal to get rich ~Jesus hates short people }

// Q5
::Q5:: From Numbers 22:1–6, 20–34, a man beats his donkey until it speaks.  
Who is this man? { =Balaam ~Saul ~Balaak ~Samuel }

// Q6
::Q6:: Jesus used parables to teach.  
Which parable did He tell about the growth of God’s kingdom? { =Mustard seed ~Prodigal son ~Lost coin ~Healing Blind Bartimaeus }

// Q7
::Q7:: Which value can help develop talents and abilities? { ~Assertiveness =Critical thinking ~Hard work ~Creative thinking }

// Q8
::Q8:: A talent is a natural gift.  
Who did God give skill and ability for artistic work? { ~Solomon =Bezalel ~Oholiab ~David }

// Q9
::Q9:: During a class discussion, you're tasked to present the Ten Commandments.  
Which commandment teaches us to speak the truth? { ~Do not kill =Do not accuse falsely ~Thou shall not covet ~Honour your father and mother }

// Q10
::Q10:: A woman who had been bleeding for twelve years was healed by touching Jesus’ cloth.  
What made her well? { ~Doctor’s medication ~Her honesty =Her faith ~Jesus rubbed mud in her eyes }

// Q11
::Q11:: Christians endure suffering for Christ’s sake.  
Which virtue did Apostle Paul practice? { =Perseverance ~Anger ~Impatience ~Dishonesty }

// Q12
::Q12:: Which temptation did Jesus face in the desert? { =Throw Himself from the pinnacle ~Change water into wine ~Stop His mission ~Deny His disciples }

// Q13
::Q13:: Which group represents the Holy Trinity? { ~Father, mother, and children =God the Father, Son, and Holy Spirit ~Jesus, Mary, and Joseph ~God the Father, Moses, and Elijah }

// Q14
::Q14:: Who was among the first four disciples called by Jesus? { =Andrew ~Judas Iscariot ~Bartholomew ~Matthew }

// Q15
::Q15:: Jesus performed many miracles.  
Which miracle shows He is the universal saviour? { ~Calming the storm ~Healing Blind Bartimaeus =Healing the Roman officer’s servant ~Raising Lazarus }

// Q16
::Q16:: Genesis 12:2 — "I will bless who bless you, but I will curse those who curse you..."  
These words were said by God to: { ~Noah ~David ~Adam =Abraham }

// Q17
::Q17:: Jacob wrestled with an Angel of God at Peniel until daybreak.  
What lesson do we learn from this story? { ~Being courageous in life =Being determined in life ~Being armed to fight ~Being humble in prayer }

// Q18
::Q18:: Christians are reminded of the need to help the needy.  
Which parable did Jesus teach about this? { =The rich man and Lazarus ~The bleeding woman ~The friend at midnight ~The unforgiving servant }

// Q19
::Q19:: Learners discussed the temptations of Jesus in Luke 4:1–13.  
Which group correctly ordered them? { =Group A (iii)(ii)(i) ~Group B (ii)(i)(iii) ~Group M (i)(iii) ~Group T (iii)(ii)(i) }

// Q20
::Q20:: What is a similarity between the birth and life of Jesus and John the Baptist? { ~Both were baptized by one person =Both births were announced by an angel ~Both parents were Joseph and Mary ~Both taught on repentance }

// Q21
::Q21:: Which cluster comprises only Old Testament books? { ~Acts, Romans, Nahum, Micah ~Exodus, Titus, Joel, James =Job, Judges, Ezra, Exodus ~Luke, Lamentations, Numbers, Jude }

// Q22
::Q22:: After reading Matthew 8:5–13 about the healing of the Roman officer’s servant, we learn all of the following *except*: { ~Employers should take care of their workers =Christians should neglect the sick ~We should have faith in God ~We should seek help from God }

// Q23
::Q23:: Which one of the following values can be used to measure honesty? { ~Respect =Integrity ~Humility ~Kindness }

// Q24
::Q24:: Who among the following recovered an axe head from the river? { =Elisha ~Elijah ~Samuel ~Nathan }

// Q25
::Q25:: What was the name of the son born to Sarah when she was ninety years old? { =Isaac ~Ishmael ~Jacob ~Joseph }

// Q26
::Q26:: Who among the following was sold to the Ishmaelites by his brothers? { =Joseph ~Benjamin ~Reuben ~Simeon }

// Q27
::Q27:: Who among the following was the first king of Israel? { =Saul ~David ~Solomon ~Rehoboam }

// Q28
::Q28:: Who among the following was a tax collector before he became a disciple of Jesus? { =Matthew ~Peter ~John ~Andrew }

// Q29
::Q29:: Who among the following was the mother of John the Baptist? { =Elizabeth ~Mary ~Martha ~Anna }

// Q30
::Q30:: Who among the following was the first Christian martyr? { =Stephen ~James ~Peter ~Paul }

// Q31
::Q31:: Who among the following was the Roman governor who sentenced Jesus to be crucified? { =Pontius Pilate ~Herod ~Caesar ~Felix }

// Q32
::Q32:: Why is the Bible an inspired word of God? { =It teaches about God ~It was written by holy men ~It is used in churches ~It is free from error }

// Q33
::Q33:: Jesus was baptized in River Jordan by? { =John ~Peter ~Jesus ~Thomas }

// Q34
::Q34:: The king of Israel that had many wives was? { =Solomon ~Saul ~David ~Jonathan }

// Q35
::Q35:: The first book in the New Testament is? { =Matthew ~Genesis ~Acts ~Revelation }

// Q36
::Q36:: Which is not a good practice for a Christian? { ~Keeping the Sabbath day Holy =Going to church ~Helping the needy ~Praising God }

// Q37
::Q37:: Which of the following was created on the third day of creation? { ~Sea and birds =Land and vegetation ~Sky and stars ~Man }

// Q38
::Q38:: Christians ought to forgive one another because? { ~It is a commandment =God forgave our sins ~It is good to forgive ~It is a promise }

// Q39
::Q39:: Which of the following is not a fruit of the Holy Spirit? { ~Humility ~Kindness =Self-control ~Patience }

// Q40
::Q40:: The following are lessons learnt from the healing of the centurion’s servant *except*: { ~Faith ~Good health =God’s help ~Care for others }

// Q41
::Q41:: Which of the following qualities was Jesus praised for by the centurion? { ~Love ~Kindness =Power ~Authority }

// Q42
::Q42:: When did Jesus go to the wilderness to be tempted by Satan? { =After baptism ~After the sermon on the mount ~After the Last Supper ~After the transfiguration }
